  "check": {
    "macOS": {
      "by_version": {},
      "default": {
        "additional_info": null,
        "result": {
          "type": "string",
          "value": "PASS"
        },
        "shell": "result=\"FAIL\"\nenabled=$(/bin/launchctl print-disabled system | /usr/bin/grep '\"org.apache.httpd\" => enabled')\nrunning=$(/bin/launchctl print system/org.apache.httpd 2>/dev/null)\n\nif [[ -z \"$running\" ]] && [[ -z \"$enabled\" ]]; then\n  result=\"PASS\"\nelif [[ -n \"$running\" ]]; then\n  result=\"${result}  RUNNING\"\nelif [[ -n \"$enabled\" ]]; then\n  result=\"${result}  ENABLED\"\nfi\necho $result"
      },
      "language": "bash"
    }
  },
  "discussion": "The built-in web server which is managed by launchd is a non-essential service built into macOS and _MUST_ be disabled and not running.\n\nNOTE: The built in web server service is disabled at startup by default macOS.\n",
